{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And you shall raise up the Mishkan.</b> Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra explained that it says this to חַכְמֵי לֵב (wise-hearted ones), etc. The Rabbi understood the totality of the commandments of HaShem and reasoned that just as all the works of the Mishkan were stated in the presence of Moses, yet after the truth he did not make them but rather the wise-hearted ones — so too would this commandment be. But this is not always so, for whatever HaShem commands in the presence of Moses, he himself does and no other — unless HaShem returns and explicitly says that others are the ones who make it; then we would say that the reason He spoke to him in His presence is to tell him that since he is the one who commands, it is as though he is the one who makes it. And like the making of the entire Mishkan and its vessels: even though He addressed the matter to him, He returned and commanded him in parashat Ki Tissa: ״קָרָאתִי בְשֵׁם בְצַלְאֵל וְגוֹ׳ וְאִתּוֹ אָהֳלִיאָב וְגוֹ׳ וּבְלֵב כָּל חֲכַם וְגוֹ׳ וְעָשׂוּ אֵת כָּל אֲשֶׁר צִוִּיתִיךָ״ — He returned and disclosed the matter, that Moses would not do any of the craftsmanship. But the raising up of the Mishkan, for which we do not find that HaShem returned and specified to him who would erect it — this tells us that the words are as written, that he himself would raise it up, and he did raise it up, as it is written (Exodus 40:18): ״וַיָּקֶם מֹשֶׁה אֶת הַמִּשְׁכָּן״ etc. — he alone and no one with him. And this is the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Shemot Rabbah 52), and it is the principal view, and apart from it the principal view is uprooted."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:45.193546550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}